.SS "uint32_t schultz_span::clickable"
Nonzero when pressing this stretch is reported to the host\&.
.PP
Separate from \fClink\fP on purpose\&. A document being shown rather than used wants its links to look like links and to copy as links without being live, and a stretch that is not a link at all may still want to be pressed: a keyword in a code editor, a name in a message, a footnote marker\&.
.PP
A press arrives as an ordinary SCHULTZ_EVENT_CLICK on the widget's node, with \fCspan\fP and \fCspan_tag\fP naming this stretch\&. The toolkit acts on none of it; what a press means is the host's business\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB103\fP of file \fBschultz_widget\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "uint64_t schultz_span::tag"
Whatever the host wants handed back when this stretch is pressed\&.
.PP
Untouched by the toolkit\&. It is how a program says which of its own things this stretch is, without keeping a table beside the span list that has to be repaired every time the text is edited\&. 
